The type 'MindmapLayoutData' doesn't exist in the types file. It should be 'LayoutData' from the generic types module.
```suggestion
import type { LayoutData, LayoutResult } from './types.js';
import type { MindmapNode } from '../../../diagrams/mindmap/mindmapTypes.js';
import type { MermaidConfig } from '../../../config.type.js';

describe('Cose-Bilkent Layout Algorithm', () => {
  let mockConfig: MermaidConfig;
  let mockRootNode: MindmapNode;
  let mockLayoutData: LayoutData;
```

We can have generic error if nodes are not present

```
if (!data.nodes || !Array.isArray(data.nodes) || data.nodes.length === 0) {
  throw new Error('No nodes found in layout data');
}
```

This is a deep import which can easisly break depending on bundler/build.

What if you do something like this instead:
```
import type { LayoutData } from 'mermaid';
...
interface NodeWithVertex extends Omit<Node, 'domId'> {
  children?: LayoutData['nodes'];
```

nit: If these 3 are the only shapes present. Ignore otherwise. 

```suggestion
  data4Layout.nodes.forEach((node) => {
    node.from = 'mindmap';
    if (node.shape === 'rounded') {
      node.radius = 15;
      node.taper = 15;
      node.stroke = 'none';
    } else if (node.shape === 'rect') {
      node.height = 46;
      node.width = 92;
    }
  });
```

Avoid spaces between imports, it messes up auto formatting. 

